---
Ingest sensor receipts under artifacts/ and render a cockpit report + comment

Usage: cockpitctl ingest [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --artifacts <ARTIFACTS>
          Artifacts directory (default: artifacts)
          
          [default: artifacts]

      --config <CONFIG>
          Policy file (default: cockpit.toml)
          
          [default: cockpit.toml]

      --label <LABEL>
          Labels present on the PR (optional; used for label-gates)

      --schema-validation <SCHEMA_VALIDATION>
          Schema validation mode for sensor receipts.
          
          - lax: Skip JSON schema validation; only parse receipts as JSON. - strict: Validate
          receipts against schemas/sensor.report.v1.json; schema violations are surfaced as findings
          rather than causing parse errors.

          Possible values:
          - lax:    Skip JSON schema validation; only parse receipts as JSON
          - strict: Validate receipts against schemas/sensor.report.v1.json

      --github-annotations
          Emit GitHub Actions workflow command annotations (::error, ::warning, ::notice) to stdout

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format for the cockpit report

          Possible values:
          - cockpit: Standard cockpit report (default)
          - sarif:   SARIF v2.1.0 (Static Analysis Results Interchange Format)
          
          [default: cockpit]

      --baseline <BASELINE>
          Path to a previous cockpit report for trend comparison

      --buildfix-auto-apply
          Enable buildfix auto-apply for this run

      --buildfix-max-auto-apply-safety <BUILDFIX_MAX_AUTO_APPLY_SAFETY>
          Maximum safety level that auto-apply may execute
          
          [possible values: safe, guarded, unsafe]

      --buildfix-actuator <BUILDFIX_ACTUATOR>
          External actuator command used for buildfix auto-apply

      --buildfix-actuator-timeout-ms <BUILDFIX_ACTUATOR_TIMEOUT_MS>
          Timeout for buildfix actuator command in milliseconds

      --disable-hooks
          Disable hook execution for this run (explicit runtime capability toggle)

      --policy-sign
          Enable policy snapshot signing for this run

      --disable-buildfix
          Disable buildfix orchestration and auto-apply for this run

      --disable-policy-signing
          Disable policy signing for this run

      --policy-sign-key-path <POLICY_SIGN_KEY_PATH>
          Override policy signing key path

      --policy-sign-key-env <POLICY_SIGN_KEY_ENV>
          Override policy signing env var name

      --policy-sign-key-id <POLICY_SIGN_KEY_ID>
          Override policy signing key identifier

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
